diff --git a/changelog.d/1756.fixed.md b/changelog.d/1756.fixed.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..0e62483
--- /dev/null
+++ b/changelog.d/1756.fixed.md
@@ -0,0 +1 @@
+- **An `if` or `match` joining an `@Int` branch with a `@Nat` branch is typed `@Int`, so the verifier obligates the narrowing** ([#1756](https://github.com/aallan/vera/issues/1756)).  The join handed the result the `@Nat` branch's type whenever that branch was the second one, so binding a `-1` sentinel beside a `@Nat` into a `@Nat` slot recorded no `nat_bind` obligation: `vera verify` accepted the program and `vera run` trapped at the emitted guard.  A mixed `@Int` / `@Nat` branch pair now takes the formal least upper bound `@Int`, whichever branch is written first, in an `if` and in a `match`; `vera verify` refuses a negative branch with E503, and a non-negative one (`-1 * -3`) records the `nat_bind` check its guard answers.
